  "what_this_shows": "Features are plentiful -- 42 to 86 per frame across the SWT planes -- and are not where the storms are. The nearest feature to a storm is a median 153.9 km away against a catalogue radius whose median is 15.2 km, and no storm of the 18 has three features within 50 km. The join required by external_reference evidence, 'matched at its own declared radius', cannot be made on this record.",
  "why": "Features here are extracted from 850 hPa TEMPERATURE. IBTrACS positions are cyclone centres defined operationally by wind and pressure. A warm core and a circulation centre need not coincide, and in a sheared or extratropically transitioning system they can be hundreds of kilometres apart. This is a property of the variable the record holds, not of the catalogue and not of the signature.",
  "what_it_does_not_show": [
    "Not that the catalogue is inadequate. It is signed, independent and correctly specified; nothing measured here bears on its labels.",
    "Not that the signature or any identity criterion fails. None was run.",
    "Not that kind_recurrence is unevaluable in principle -- only that it is unevaluable against THIS record, whose single variable is 850 hPa temperature.",
    "Nothing about D96 to D100, a mining radius, or T4E.8's acceptance."
  ],
  "what_would_unblock_it": "A record variable in which a cyclone centre is an extractable feature -- relative vorticity, mean sea level pressure, or 10 m wind speed. That is a new CDS acquisition and a new record, and it is the maintainer's decision, not a consequence of this measurement.",
  "claim_boundary": "Synthetic and acquired evidence settle properties of the instrument, not of the atmosphere. No frame of the 2022-2023 forecast-test period was opened."
}